---
import type { Locale } from '../../i18n';
import { localePath } from '../../i18n';

interface Props { locale: Locale }
const { locale } = Astro.props;
const zh = locale === 'zh';
const t = (cn: string, en: string) => zh ? cn : en;

const steps = [
  {
    index: 'N1',
    title: t('先验证纠错后的 128 题真的和 SEED 官方运行路径一致', 'First verify the corrected 128 tasks against the authoritative SEED runtime path'),
    plain: t(
      '我们已经先把 SEED 真正会看到的 128 个任务重建出来，但更严格的审计又发现：第一版重建漏掉了一个会改变题目顺序的随机种子细节。那一版已经作废并重新生成。现在不继续往下跑模型，而是先用真实的 WebshopWorker 运行路径逐题检查新版；只有 128/128 都一致，BASE 与 OpenEvo 的正式比较才重新放行。这里仍然不是在声称找回论文 89.7 / 78.1% 当年使用的最终 128 题。',
      'We already reconstructed the 128 tasks that a specified released-code validation would see, but a stricter audit found that the first reconstruction missed a random-seed detail that changes goal ordering. That manifest was superseded and rebuilt. The current step is not more model execution: validate every corrected task through the real WebshopWorker runtime path. Only a 128/128 match reopens the formal BASE-vs-OpenEvo comparison. This still does not claim recovery of the paper-final 128 tasks behind 89.7 / 78.1%.',
    ),
    technical: t(
      '专业解释：两次干净构建必须得到相同 canonical hash，这一 deterministic rebuild gate 已经通过；随后发现 pinned SEED SimServer 会在 synthetic goals 构造后、shuffle 前再次 random.seed(worker_seed)，旧 builder 漏掉了这一步。corrected manifest 已重新物化，当前状态回到 PREPARED / formal_task_consumption_allowed=false；下一道门是 authoritative WebshopWorker runtime semantic validation 128/128。BASE 与 OpenEvo SD-LoRA 都保持冻结。',
      'Technical detail: two clean builds must produce the same canonical hash, and that deterministic rebuild gate has passed. A later audit found that pinned SEED SimServer reseeds with random.seed(worker_seed) after synthetic-goal construction and before shuffle; the previous builder omitted that step. The corrected manifest has been rematerialized and the state is back to PREPARED / formal_task_consumption_allowed=false. The next gate is authoritative WebshopWorker runtime semantic validation at 128/128. BASE and OpenEvo SD-LoRA remain frozen.',
    ),
  },
  {
    index: 'N2',
    title: t('再解决第二代“学新东西时把旧能力弄丢”', 'Then address second-generation forgetting'),
    plain: t(
      '第二次更新不是没有新经验，而是模型在吸收新经验时，没有同时稳定保住原来会做的任务和第一代已经得到的提升。',
      'The second update did have new experience. The problem is that learning it did not stably preserve both prior capability and the first-generation gain.',
    ),
    technical: t(
      '专业解释：下一轮机制实验会围绕经验回放（experience replay）和正则化（regularization），同时重新测试新经验获取（acquisition）、旧能力保持（retention）和已有收益保持（preservation）。',
      'Technical detail: the next mechanism study should use experience replay and regularization while retesting acquisition, retention, and preservation together.',
    ),
  },
  {
    index: 'N3',
    title: t('最后再去 ALFWorld 看这个现象是不是 WebShop 特有', 'Then test whether the effect is specific to WebShop'),
    plain: t(
      '如果 WebShop 上的一次迁移和多次连续更新都变得稳定，再把同样的问题搬到 ALFWorld。这样才能判断我们看到的是通用学习现象，还是只适用于 WebShop 的任务结构。',
      'If one-step transfer and repeated updating become stable on WebShop, carry the same questions to ALFWorld to test whether the finding generalizes beyond WebShop-specific task structure.',
    ),
    technical: t(
      '专业解释：跨环境复现（cross-environment replication）应该在 WebShop 的关键结论稳定以后进行，否则会把“方法机制不稳定”和“环境差异”两个变量混在一起。',
      'Technical detail: cross-environment replication should follow stable WebShop mechanism evidence; otherwise method instability and environment differences would be confounded.',
    ),
  },
] as const;
---

<section class="next-steps" id="next-steps" aria-labelledby="next-steps-title">
  <header class="section-heading">
    <p>{t('下一步实验 · NEXT STEPS', 'NEXT STEPS')}</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="next-steps-title">{t('下一场真正会改变结论的实验', 'The next experiment that can change the conclusion')}</h2>
      <p class="plain-intro">{t(
        '最优先的事情不是继续调模型，而是先确认纠错后的 128 题和固定版本 SEED 公开代码的真实运行路径逐题一致。这个验证通过以后，才重新放行 BASE 与 OpenEvo 的正式比较。',
        'The highest-priority step is not more model tuning. First verify that the corrected 128 tasks match the real runtime path of the pinned SEED public code, one task at a time. Only after that passes should the formal BASE-vs-OpenEvo comparison be released again.',
      )}</p>
      <p class="technical-intro"><strong>{t('专业解释：', 'Technical detail: ')}</strong>{t(
        '历史 128-task panel 仍然只是冻结的本地 SEED-compatible 面板。新的 source-faithful 路线已经完成 panel 重建，但第一版 manifest 因 SimServer reseed 语义遗漏而被 superseded；corrected manifest 尚未通过 authoritative runtime 128/128 gate，因此当前不能发布新的 BASE-vs-SD 结果。公开信息依然不足以唯一恢复论文最终表格对应的 validation 次序与 checkpoint。',
        'The historical 128-task panel remains a frozen local SEED-compatible panel. The source-faithful track has now rebuilt its panel, but the first manifest was superseded after a missing SimServer reseed semantic was found. The corrected manifest has not yet passed the authoritative runtime 128/128 gate, so no new BASE-vs-SD result may be published. Public information still does not uniquely recover the validation ordinal and checkpoint behind the paper-final table.',
      )}</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <ol class="step-list">
    {steps.map((step) => (
      <li class="step-card">
        <span class="step-index">{step.index}</span>
        <div>
          <h3>{step.title}</h3>
          <p class="step-plain">{step.plain}</p>
          <p class="step-technical">{step.technical}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <aside class="min-gap">
    <strong>{t('两条后续路线回答不同问题', 'Two follow-up tracks answer different questions')}</strong>
    <p>{t(
      '路线 A（Track A）问：能不能忠实复现 SEED 公开代码能恢复出来的一次指定验证任务语义？现在它正处在 corrected panel 的运行时 128/128 验证门。路线 B（Track B，WB1）问：在同一个冻结世界、同一套任务、同一评测程序和匹配预算下，把 SEED 方法本身与 OpenEvo 重新跑一遍，谁表现更好？只有路线 B 才能真正回答 OpenEvo vs SEED，而不是把我们的数字直接和论文 89.7 / 78.1% 相减。',
      'Track A asks whether task semantics for a specified validation call recoverable from released SEED code can be reproduced faithfully; it is now at the corrected-panel 128/128 runtime-validation gate. Track B (WB1) asks which method performs better after rerunning the SEED method itself and OpenEvo under one frozen world, the same tasks, the same evaluator, and matched budgets. Only Track B directly answers OpenEvo vs SEED; it does not subtract our number from the paper’s 89.7 / 78.1%.',
    )} <a href={localePath(locale, '/research/seed-openevo/experiment/')}>{t('查看实验设定 ↗', 'See the experiment setup ↗')}</a></p>
  </aside>
</section>

<style>
  .next-steps{max-width:1160px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px 52px;color:var(--color-text)}
  .section-heading{display:grid;grid-template-columns:145px minmax(0,760px);gap:28px;padding:38px 0 24px;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)}
  .section-heading>p{margin:5px 0 0;color:var(--color-text-muted);font-size:.73rem;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.1em}
  .section-heading h2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:clamp(1.55rem,3vw,2.5rem);line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-.035em}
  .section-heading div>p{margin:0;max-width:70ch;font-size:.94rem;line-height:1.68}
  .plain-intro{color:var(--color-text)}
  .technical-intro{margin-top:9px!important;padding-top:9px;border-top:1px dashed var(--color-border);color:var(--color-text-muted);font-size:.82rem!important}
  .technical-intro strong{color:var(--color-text)}
  .step-list{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:10px}
  .step-card{display:grid;grid-template-columns:62px minmax(0,1fr);gap:20px;padding:22px 24px;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:15px;background:var(--color-bg)}
  .step-index{color:var(--color-accent);font:700 .82rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}
  .step-card h3{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:1.05rem;letter-spacing:-.02em}
  .step-card p{margin:0;max-width:78ch;line-height:1.68}
  .step-plain{color:var(--color-text);font-size:.87rem}
  .step-technical{margin-top:8px!important;padding-top:8px;border-top:1px dashed var(--color-border);color:var(--color-text-muted);font-size:.78rem}
  .min-gap{margin-top:12px;padding:18px 22px;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);border-radius:0 12px 12px 0;background:var(--color-surface)}
  .min-gap>strong{display:block;margin-bottom:5px;font-size:.86rem}
  .min-gap p{margin:0;max-width:84ch;font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.66}
  .min-gap a{color:var(--color-accent);font-weight:750;text-decoration:none}
  .min-gap a:hover{text-decoration:underline}
  @media(max-width:720px){
    .next-steps{padding-inline:18px}
    .section-heading{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px}
    .step-card{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px;padding:18px}
  }
</style>